    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Focal epilepsy on levetiracetam (G40.209)</content>. Seizure-free for four weeks; early irritability has settled. PHQ-9 4, item 9 scored 0. [S]<list><item>Continue levetiracetam 500 mg twice daily.</item><item>Seizure diary.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Chronic left temporal cortical infarct (I69.398)</content>. More than 40 days of monitoring without atrial fibrillation, so aspirin, not an anticoagulant, is right. No sleep apnea. MoCA 28 of 30: normal. [S]<list><item>Continue aspirin 81 mg and atorvastatin 80 mg.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Hypertension (I10)</content>. 136/84 mmHg in the office and 134/84 mmHg at home on lisinopril 10 mg: above target. [S]<list><item>Add amlodipine 5 mg daily; ankle swelling explained.</item><item>Continue the home log.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Acute viral upper respiratory infection (J06.9)</content>. Resolved without complications; no seizure during it. [S]<list><item>No further action.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Blood pressure (target below 130/80 mmHg)</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>136/84 mmHg; home average 134/84 mmHg; amlodipine added</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Home blood pressure monitoring</td><td>Daily while treatment is adjusted</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Two weeks of stored readings reviewed</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>Ambulatory rhythm monitoring for atrial fibrillation</td><td>At least 30 days within six months of the event</td><td>Completed today</td><td>More than 40 days in all; no atrial fibrillation</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Sleep apnea evaluation</td><td>Consider after any stroke</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Home sleep test: apnea-hypopnea index 4 per hour; no sleep apnea</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Depression screen (PHQ-9)</td><td>At the first visit after the event, then periodically</td><td>Completed today</td><td>4; item 9 scored 0</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Cognitive screen (MoCA)</td><td>In the first year after a stroke</td><td>Completed today</td><td>28 of 30</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Lipid panel after starting a statin</td><td>4 to 12 weeks after starting</td><td>Due</td><td>At the ten-week visit</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Statin tolerance</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No muscle aches</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Antithrombotic adherence and bleeding</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Aspirin taken daily; no bruising or bleeding</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Antiseizure medicine: seizures, adherence, and side effects</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No seizure; irritability in the first week only; no missed doses</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Fall risk</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No falls</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Weight and BMI</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>75.6 kg; BMI 22.8</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Tobacco, alcohol, physical activity, and diet</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Diet changes kept up; walking daily; alcohol unchanged</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Seizure safety and driving</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Not driving; riding only with a companion; seizure-free for four weeks</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>Cause of the spells established and explained to him by the neurology visit. Outcome by 2026-08-18: Focal epilepsy with a structural vascular cause, from a chronic left temporal cortical infarct; syncope and transient ischemic attack judged unlikely [S]</item><item>No seizures on levetiracetam through the ten-week review. In progress; target 2026-10-27 [S]</item><item>Office blood pressure below 130/80 mmHg. In progress; target 2026-10-27 [S]</item><item>LDL cholesterol below 70 mg/dL on a high-intensity statin. In progress; target 2026-10-27 [S]</item><item>No driving, swimming alone, or riding alone while the seizure-free period is counted, with a written seizure action plan for his staff. In progress; target 2026-10-27 [S]</item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: Practice guideline update summary: Efficacy and tolerability of the new antiepileptic drugs I: Treatment of new-onset epilepsy (2018); 2021 Guideline for the Prevention of Stroke in Patients With Stroke and Transient Ischemic Attack (2021); 2025 AHA/ACC/AANP/AAPA/ABC/ACCP/ACPM/AGS/AMA/ASPC/NMA/PCNA/SGIM Guideline for the Prevention, Detection, Evaluation and Management of High Blood Pressure in Adults (2025); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, stroke and transient ischemic attack, hypertension, and hyperlipidemia monographs (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Adult preventive visit in three weeks; ten-week chronic-care review with the lipid panel. Next scheduled visit 2026-10-06: adult preventive visit. [S]</paragraph></text>

